/(q+1), the EXCISED convention C. The regression witness is also convention C (G[0][1] = 0.4993203341836944) but at the proton pin. Under the CANONICAL convention D the same object (computations/gram-matrix-dual.witness.json, z = 0.6126880371464652, proton pin) has spectrum {4.2303392, 0.7527021132519656 x3, 3.07e-17, -0.7527021132519656}: the block's lambda_- should read -0.7527, not -0.855, and only under D is the name 'lambda_0' literally correct (it is 0.1018, not zero, under C). (4) UNSUPPORTED COMPARATIVE: the mirror word's |Delta net| = 0.004 is called 'an order of magnitude worse', but the comparison target is 0.000 (against which no ratio is defined) and the block's own next bullet puts all other words above 0.01, i.e. 0.004 is 2.5x BETTER than that floor, not an order of magnitude worse. State what it is worse than, or drop the comparative.","history":3},{"id":"trap-performed-warmth","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:g01","notes":"Institutional register.","history":2},{"id":"trap-rhetorical-pivot","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:g01","notes":"Clean.","history":2},{"id":"trap-superlative","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:g01","notes":"See trap-nonspeakable notes for the one unsupported comparative, recorded there as a math finding rather than as style inflation.","history":2},{"id":"trap-thesis-restatement","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:g01","notes":"No restating closer.","history":2},{"id":"trap-triples","group":"trap","result":"pass","stale":true,"freshness":"stale","changed":["md","ts"],"at":"2026-08-22","reviewer":"agent","by":"agent:g01","notes":"Th